[section:latches Latches]

A latch is a synchronization mechanism used to wait until a specified number
of events have occurred. A latch is initialized with a counter, which is
decremented by calls to [member_link latch..count_down] or
[member_link latch..arrive_and_wait]. When the counter reaches zero, the latch
is opened and all fibers waiting on the latch can proceed.

A latch can be thought of as a single-use [class_link barrier]. Unlike a barrier, a
latch is not reset after the counter reaches zero. Once opened, the latch
remains open for its lifetime, and subsequent calls to [member_link
latch..wait] return immediately.

Barriers and latches are useful for different synchronization patterns.
Barriers are useful when a group of fibers must repeatedly synchronize at a
common point. Latches are useful when a group of work items must be completed
before proceeding, without requiring the work to be performed by particular
execution agent or in a particular order.

[class_heading latch]

        #include <boost/fiber/latch.hpp>

        namespace boost {
        namespace fibers {

        class latch {
        public:
            explicit latch( std::size_t initial);

            latch( latch const&) = delete;
            latch & operator=( latch const&) = delete;
            latch( latch &&) = delete;
            latch & operator=( latch &&) = delete;
            ~latch() = default;

            void count_down( std::size_t n = 1);
            void wait();
            void arrive_and_wait( std::size_t n = 1);
        };

        }}

Instances of __latch__ are not copyable or movable.

A latch maintains a counter that is initialized by the constructor.
The counter can be decremented by calling `count_down` or
`arrive_and_wait`. The latch is opened when the counter reaches zero.

[heading Constructor]

        explicit latch( std::size_t initial);

[variablelist
[[Effects:] [Constructs a latch with its counter initialized to `initial`.]]
]

[heading Destructor]

        ~latch();

[variablelist
[[Effects:] [Destroys the latch.]]
[[Precondition:] [No fiber is waiting on `*this`.  Either no `wait` or `arrive_and_wait`
were called or the latch counter has reached zero.]]
]

[member_heading latch..count_down]

        void count_down( std::size_t n = 1);

[variablelist
[[Effects:] [Atomically decrements the latch counter by `n`. If the counter
reaches zero, all fibers blocked in `wait` or `arrive_and_wait` are
unblocked.]]
[[Requires:] [`n` is greater than zero and less than or equal to the current
latch counter.]]
]

[member_heading latch..try_wait]

        bool wait() const;

[variablelist
[[Returns:] [`true` if the latch counter has reached zero, `false` otherwise.
The check is performed atomically.]]
]

[member_heading latch..wait]

        void wait();

[variablelist
[[Effects:] [Blocks the calling fiber until the latch counter reaches zero.
Returns immediately if the counter is already zero.]]
]

[member_heading latch..arrive_and_wait]

        void arrive_and_wait( std::size_t n = 1);

[variablelist
[[Effects:] [Decrements the latch counter by `n`. If the counter reaches zero,
all fibers blocked in `wait` or `arrive_and_wait` are unblocked.
Otherwise, blocks the calling fiber until the latch counter reaches zero.]]
[[Requires:] [`n` is greater than zero and less than or equal to the current
latch counter.]]
]

[endsect]
